  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- `assets/posts/haas.cps`, `ff()`: the F word keeps its fraction. An mm feed has up to three decimals. An inch feed has up to four decimals (it had two). The post trims the trailing zeros and always writes the point (`F600.`, `F34.5`, `F133.2`, `F1.3583`). One formatter writes each Haas feed, not only G84.\r\n- `assets/posts/haas.cps`, new `tapPitchHolds()`, called in `onCycle()` for G84: the post compares the pitch of the written words (F / S) with the stream pitch (feed / rpm). If the difference is more than 0.01 percent of the pitch, the post refuses the cycle by name through `msg()`. It writes no partial block.\r\n- `docs/decisions/3694-haas-tap-feed-exact.md`: the options, the option taken, the source of the feed format (Haas Mill Operator's Manual 96-8000, Setting 77) and the worst case of the residual pitch error.\r\n\r\n## Readings (before -> after)\r\n\r\n| Case | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| G84, mm, 34.5 mm/min at S115 (M1.4 x 0.3) | `F35.` | `F34.5` |\r\n| G84, mm, 133.2 mm/min at S333 (M2 x 0.4) | `F133.` | `F133.2` |\r\n| G84, inch, 34.5 mm/min at S115 | `F1.36` | `F1.3583` |\r\n| G84, inch, 635 mm/min at S500 (1/4-20) | `F25.` | `F25.` |\r\n| G1, mm, 50.8 mm/min | `F51.` | `F50.8` |\r\n| G1, mm, 12.4 mm/min | `F12.` | `F12.4` |\r\n| G84, inch, 2 mm/min at S100 | `F0.08` (1.6 percent off) | refused by name |\r\n| G84, mm, 34.5 mm/min at 115.4 rpm (written S115) | `F35.` | refused by name |\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n`crates/post/tests/haas_feed_decimal_point.rs`:\r\n\r\n- `haas_g84_writes_the_exact_tap_feed_in_mm` (new)\r\n- `haas_g84_writes_the_tap_feed_at_four_inch_decimals` (new)\r\n- `haas_refuses_a_tap_pitch_its_words_cannot_hold` (new)\r\n- `haas_keeps_the_fraction_of_an_mm_feed` (new, 12.4 mm/min, #3692)\r\n- `crates/app/tests/program_units.rs` `every_inch_post_writes_the_mm_program_in_inches`, with the two new Haas inch goldens.\r\n- `haas_writes_every_mm_feed_word_with_its_point`: the pin at line 210 changed from `F51.` to `F50.8`. This is the intended change.\r\n\r\nThe five tests are red with the `haas.cps` of `origin/main` (`F35.` for `F34.5`, `F1.36` for `F1.3583`) and green with the fix.\r\n\r\n## Quick gate (head 30c4c7ef0)\r\n\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post` (whole crate, `--no-fail-fast`): all binaries pass.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app` with `--test` for `conformance`, `rigid_tapping`, `tap_hand`, `post_cycle_feed_spindle`, `fine_bore_cycle`, `control_comp`, `wear_comp`, `program_entry`, `golden_cl`, `example_catalog`: all pass.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- Review fix, run on head 30c4c7ef0: `cargo test -p camcraft-app` with `--test program_units`, `--test post_unit_word`, `--test program_info` and `--test conformance`, and `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test haas_feed_decimal_point`. All pass.\r\n- The mm goldens did not change. They hold only whole feeds (`tap_plate.nc` `F750.`, `synth_haas.nc` `F240.`).\r\n- Two Haas inch goldens changed: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/haas/contour_plate_with_hole.nc` and `drill_peck.nc`. `program_units` was red before the new files were written (`every_inch_post_writes_the_mm_program_in_inches`). The new files come from `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test program_units`. A script compared them with the old files. Only F words changed (43 words). Each new value is within 0.005 of the old value. No golden of another post changed.\r\n\r\n| Inch golden line | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `contour_plate_with_hole.nc`, cutting moves (500 mm/min) | `F19.69` | `F19.685` |\r\n| `contour_plate_with_hole.nc`, plunges (100 mm/min) | `F3.94` | `F3.937` |\r\n| `drill_peck.nc:16`, cycle feed (60 mm/min) | `F2.36` | `F2.3622` |\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/program_units.rs`: the doc of `same_program_in_inch` and the F tolerance comment now say that Haas writes four in/min decimals. The bound of 0.005 in/min stays: it holds for each post.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The heavy lane was not run. The targeted heavy step for `conformance` holds 0 tests.\r\n- No Haas control read the new F words. The number of decimals that the control accepts in F was not checked on a machine. Three (mm) and four (inch) are the steps of the post's other words.\r\n- The other six mill posts are not changed. Issue #3699 holds them.\r\n\r\n## Note on #3692\r\n\r\nThis PR does each point of #3692 for Haas: a decision on the mm feed precision with its source, and a test that posts a fractional mm feed (12.4 mm/min) and a tap feed. The two Haas inch goldens above are written again.\r\n\r\nChangelog: fix - The Haas post writes each feed with its decimals (three in mm/min, four in in/min), so a G84 tap feed gives the exact thread pitch; a tap whose written F and S cannot give the pitch within 0.01 percent is refused by name.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #3692\r\nFixes #3694\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
